# 5. LOCAL SCANNING SECURITY MODEL

Do NOT attempt to silently access the user's filesystem.

The system must use explicit user authorization.

Preferred architecture:

```text
Browser
   │
   ▼
Qguard Helix Local Scanner
Web UI
   │
   ▼
Local Scanner Agent
   │
   ├── Filesystem Access
   ├── Git Access
   ├── Local Tooling
   ├── Source Analysis
   └── Crypto Analysis
```

The Local Scanner Agent should run locally on the user's device.

Possible implementation:

```text
qguard-helix-local-agent
```

Support:

* Windows
* Linux
* macOS

The agent should expose a localhost-only authenticated API.

Example:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:<dynamic-port>
```

Prefer:

* Loopback binding
* Random/dynamic port
* Short-lived authentication token
* Origin validation
* Request signing
* Job authorization
* Strict filesystem sandboxing

Do NOT expose the local scanner agent to:

```text
0.0.0.0
```

unless explicitly configured and secured.

Never require users to expose their filesystem scanner publicly.

